course: dictionary
lesson: 7460
title: Popular: liked and chosen by many
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Popular» means liked by many people, or chosen by many people. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. In «Oriental fire-bellied toads are popular pets», the clue is pets: many people like to keep them.
explain: The word can also mean believed or chosen by many people, as in «a popular choice» or «a popular idea». Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try "liked by many" in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Popular is not the same as kind or good. A popular person is liked by many people, but it is good to have a few real friends too. On a tally chart or bar chart, the most popular choice is the one with the biggest count.
fact: Popular means liked by many people, or chosen by many people.
fact: «A popular choice» is one that lots of people pick.
fact: In maths, the mode is the most popular value: the one that appears most often.
fact: «Pop music» is short for popular music, music made for ordinary people, not experts.
fact: Popular is an adjective: popular, more popular, most popular.
exercise: «Oriental fire-bellied toads are popular pets, and hands must be washed after touching them.» What does popular mean here? | *Liked by many people as pets | Made only by experts | Very loud and noisy | Dangerous to touch
exercise: On a tally chart of favourite sports, football has the biggest count. What is the most popular choice on this chart? | *The one with the biggest count | The one nobody picked | The one with the smallest count | The one written first
exercise: Mia says popular means the same as kind. Is she right? | *No, a popular person is liked by many, which is not the same as kind | No, popular means very old | Yes, popular and kind always mean the same thing | Yes, but only at school
test: «The skipping game was popular with the Year 5 children.» What does popular with mean? | Ignored by | *Liked by | Tired of
test: On a bar chart, which choice is the most popular? | The bar with no colour | The bar with the lowest count | The bar at the far left | *The bar with the biggest count
exam: Which phrase means music made for ordinary people, not experts? | *pop music | jazz solo | classical symphony | opera singer
